KG42.register("clusters-a9f40ac85ee48aa74789c2e0",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v142-d-CL001","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","label":"Bilateral bidding, price negotiation, and welfare clearing under fixed roles","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Bilateral bidding, price negotiation, and welfare clearing under fixed roles","market_meaning":"Each agent updates bilateral quantities according to local costs, product differentiation coefficients, roles, and power bounds, and exchanges quantity and price estimates with trading neighbors. RCI combines quantity feedback, price coordination, and local decisions to achieve welfare clearing under reciprocity constraints upon convergence; the current frozen chains do not yet constitute complete implementation rules with mathematical closure.","mechanism_ids":["M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination","participation","matching"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"R001—R004 belong to the same M01 base MBED and RCI process. R006 supports the consumer branch of the base model only through the consumer role in the two-bus case; the case scope is not extended to all participants. R005 serves as shared background indicating that the study adopts a complete communication graph and is not elevated to a necessary condition for all MBED implementations. R001-C003 and R002-C003 are retained as comparison cases involving direct solution of the local problem, not as behavioral requirements for RCI projection updates. This cluster does not cover physical network reliability, real-time balancing, or the optional prosumer extension.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Assembled on the basis of source-supported relationships among bilateral quantity and price feedback, local quantity decisions, and the overall clearing objective, spanning bidding, coordination, clearing, and role conditions. Negotiation permission has an independent meaning, while prosumer splitting and the tax-and-fee interpretation have additional conditions, so they are retained separately.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides consumer quantity decisions, price inputs, feasibility restrictions, and communication obligations, constituting the demand branch in negotiation feedback."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides producer quantity updates and communication obligations, participating in bilateral negotiation together with the demand branch; its missing mathematical objects remain explicitly unresolved."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the shared clearing objective and reciprocity, role, and power-bound constraints, supplying outcome semantics for local negotiation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Connects quantity feedback from both parties, price estimates, information exchange, and the stopping process, carrying the RCI coordination activities."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Supplements the correspondence between consumer roles and quantity symbols within its two-bus case scope, without being counted as a separate quantity update rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"Indicates only that trading neighbors in the study come from a complete market communication graph; the primary assignment of its negotiation permission remains in a separate cluster."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x-lambda-nm","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambda","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambdahat","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"],"rationale":"The trading price estimate held by the same consumer becomes an input to the quantity update after adjustment by the local differentiation coefficient. This correspondence concerns the price and decision interface; it neither merges the trading price with the perceived price nor adds the update sequence as a new scientific edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-Pnm","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x-P-nm","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"],"rationale":"The current bilateral quantity sent by the consumer corresponds to the own-side quantity used in the price update; the counterparty quantity remains a separate object and cannot be directly replaced by the own-side quantity before convergence."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x-lambda-nm","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"],"rationale":"The producer performs its quantity update using the perceived price following the price update, retaining the producer projection branch. R002 contains only procedural objects; this connection does not invent its missing variables, parameters, or update formulas."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"],"rationale":"The producer's obligation to communicate supply quantities and the supply quantity feedback in the coordination chain are complementary activities within the same negotiation process; the procedural description is not presented as a complete mathematical model of the producer."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g02-e30"],"rationale":"The source presents RCI as a decentralized implementation of MBED, using the innovation term to address reciprocity constraints and the consensus term to coordinate the two parties' price estimates for the same trade. Correspondence with the welfare optimum is conditional on actual convergence and cannot be established directly from the existing stopping expression."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-Pnm","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-Pn","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::P_nm","v141-c-R003::x::P_n","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e17"],"rationale":"Consumers' bilateral requests and aggregate net injections correspond to the consumer subdomain of the overall MBED decisions. The quantity iteration process and the final feasible clearing state are retained separately, without claiming that aggregate bounds are satisfied at every iteration."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::Omega_p","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e32"],"rationale":"The sign and aggregate-bound obligations in the supply chain correspond to the producer branch of the overall clearing constraints; sign projection at each iteration and the treatment of power bounds through Lagrangian relaxation remain distinguished as different approaches."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27"],"rationale":"The base role restrictions specify the applicability conditions of the consumer quantity branch, under which the consumers in the case can be interpreted. This does not make the case scope of R006 identical to the general consumer scope of R001, nor are its role constraints deduplicated against the projection update as a whole."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL001-L009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::omega_n","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g01-e05"],"rationale":"The complete communication graph explains the market meaning of the neighbor set in the study. This is a scenario correspondence; it does not turn permission to negotiate into an obligation to transact, nor does it imply physical grid connections or the impossibility of models beyond complete graphs."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g01-e33"],"rationale":"These references point to the price coordination function linking bidding and clearing within the same M01, with R004 selected as the display representative. Node identity correspondence does not imply that all trading prices, the two parties' iterative estimates, or perceived prices have identical numerical values; the original objects in each chain remain retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e19"],"rationale":"The same consumer bilateral request function appears in local decisions and coordination feedback; only the node display is unified, without merging edges of different directions or types in the two chains."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M003","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"],"rationale":"The same producer supply function serves quantity updating and the provision of feedback to the coordination process; the original chains and distinct scientific edges all remain accessible."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-Pnm","v141-c-R003::x::P_nm","v141-c-R004::x::x-P-nm","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27"],"rationale":"For the same consumer n, neighbor m, and corresponding iteration indices, they represent the demand decision, overall decision, coordination state, and case-role representation of the same directed bilateral quantity. The association applies only to the common consumer subdomain; iterative values are not equivalent to final clearing values, the case is not extended to all participants, and the quantity in the counterparty direction is not included."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-Pn","v141-c-R003::x::P_n"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06"],"rationale":"The aggregate net injection of the same consumer corresponds across the demand chain and the overall clearing chain. The consumer-specific scope and the overall agent scope are retained, without conflating the aggregate quantity with any individual bilateral quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambda","v141-c-R004::x::x-lambda-nm"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e19"],"rationale":"After aligning the consumer, trading direction, and iteration state, the two correspond to the trading price estimate held by agent n. R001 uses it as an input to the decision step, while R004 treats it as an endogenously updated variable; the local types and roles are both retained, without merging it with the counterparty estimate or the perceived price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-an","v141-c-R003::theta::a_n"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09"],"rationale":"The quadratic cost coefficient of the same agent is used respectively in calculating the consumer objective and in the overall cost objective. The shared source definition supports quantity correspondence, but the applicability conditions required for the inverse gradient still need further verification."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M008","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-bn","v141-c-R003::theta::b_n"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09"],"rationale":"The linear cost coefficient of the same agent corresponds across the local decision and the overall objective, retaining the respective parameter objects and their scopes of application."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M009","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-cnm","v141-c-R003::theta::c_nm"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e28"],"rationale":"After aligning the same agent perspective and the same directed trade, the coefficient in the bilateral cost objective corresponds to the coefficient in the perceived price adjustment. Their different uses as an objective coefficient and a local input are retained, without inferring that the two parties' coefficients are equal or that all coefficients represent taxes or fees."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL001-M010","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e19"],"rationale":"Both entries require consumers to send the same set of quantity and price information to neighbors at each iteration, with identical entities, timing, and obligation scope. The consumer communication entry in R004 serves as the display representative, while the original constraint and binding in R001 remain retained; they are not counted twice as two communication obligations."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence used in this cluster remains unverified; the experiment permits candidate use, but no B source audit, independent C2 review, or Agent E review has been conducted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently conduct manual, item-by-item checks of the original text, symbols, and scope used in this cluster; retain the candidate and not independently verified flags until these checks are complete."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G002","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The C2 candidate for R002 was not adopted, and there are currently no variable or parameter objects; the producer objective and quantity updates remain procedural entries. Quantity objects from other chains cannot substitute for the complete mathematical bindings missing from this chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream must explicitly revise the producer mathematical objects, scope, and C2 bindings, and resolve the original C2_unbound_math_object issue; D does not infer replacement content."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G003","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R001-C001 uses the target power P_{n(m)}, but its variable references include only the bilateral quantity P_nm; the two cannot be treated as the same quantity merely because they are related. The target expression also divides by a_n, whereas the existing parameter domain includes a_n=0, and the typesetting, overbars, and underbars in the text of Eq. (18) remain unresolved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X-Pnm","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-an","v141-c-R003::theta::a_n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g03-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original version of the target expression, distinguish the target aggregate power from the bilateral update quantity, and supply the correct object references; specify the strictly positive coefficient condition under which the inverse gradient applies or a treatment of zero coefficients supported by the source."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Although bound multipliers exist as R001 inputs, the current chain does not fully represent the recurrences in Eqs. (12)—(13) and η^k; δ^k in Eq. (20) and the quantity iteration indices also lack complete declarations. The μ_n in the R004 stopping entry lacks a corresponding state object, the net injection domain in R003 contains confusion between upper- and lower-bound symbols, and the bounds in the objective constraints are not fully declared in its parameter references.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-mubar","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-mulow","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-fnm","v141-c-R003::x::P_n","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R004::theta::theta-epsilon-mu","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e25","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g02-e08","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the upper and lower power bounds, multiplier correspondences, and update notation, and have C clarify the assignment, conditions, and object references of the bound recurrences and weighting parameters; keep the currently frozen expressions unchanged, and do not present inputs shared across chains as complete recurrences."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R004-C008 and the current B text record a signed-difference threshold, which cannot yet be identified as an absolute-difference or norm criterion; even a large negative change alone may satisfy the listed inequality, so convergence cannot be confirmed on this basis. Criterion (26) is explicitly optional. Descriptions of stopping based on absolute changes or optimality gaps in proposals awaiting approval cannot be inserted into the existing chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008","v141-c-R004::theta::theta-epsilon-lambda","v141-c-R004::theta::theta-epsilon-P","v141-c-R004::theta::theta-epsilon-mu"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e34","v141-b-g03-E01"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-p4","v141-b-g03-EP03"],"required_work":"Check the absolute values, norms, indices, and joint stopping conditions in Eqs. (24)—(26), and distinguish iteration stopping from ex post optimality-gap assessment; do not add absolute values or change the criterion to gap-based stopping without authorization."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G006","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The current evidence includes both passages claiming a single optimum on the basis of convexity and statements that bilateral allocations admit multiple solutions when the communication graph is complete and product differentiation is absent. Positive aggregate cost curvature does not automatically guarantee uniqueness of all bilateral decisions; a persistent excitation condition alone also cannot complete the convergence proof. This cluster does not guarantee a unique bilateral allocation or exact optimality at finite stopping.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-e03","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream must separately clarify the uniqueness of the objective value, aggregate decisions, and bilateral allocations, as well as the conditions under which feasibility and convergence apply; retain case-specific tuning values and numerical validation results within the scope of the case."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL001-G007","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The formation of cost coefficients from product criteria, perceived prices, reciprocity constraints, and the RCI communication process are currently dispersed across existing parameters and constraints, and no complete independent pricing chain exists yet. The related node proposals remain unapproved and cannot serve as a basis for introducing new nodes, uniform regional prices, or a central coordinator.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-cnm","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambdahat","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-01","v141-b-g01-prop-02","v141-b-g01-prop-03","v141-b-g01-prop-04","v141-b-g02-p2","v141-b-g02-p3","v141-b-g02-p5","v141-b-g03-EP02","v141-b-g03-EP03"],"required_work":"Manually review the semantic boundaries and duplication relationships of these proposals, and have upstream determine whether criterion parameters, price conditions, and their graph bindings need to be supplemented; D retains only the existing references."}]},"rule_refs":["13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001","13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002","13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R003","13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004","13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R006","13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","COMP-a774da994c2ca212","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","KG31-95bb253080ce87de"]});
